  "leftDirty": true,
  "answer": "A third Enter takes the marks off: * a, blank, then b; a quote's bare > goes too. Backspace on a new number or quote takes the whole mark. Enter mid line carries the rest under a new mark. Enter at a bullet's start only adds a line above. A long line wraps under one line number, and the active-line band covers all of it. In the Code Editor view Link's popover sits 6 below the button, a link written there waits for Close, and Escape closes the view with the panel left open and the text carried over."
}
